WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:48.000
How would you do this today? Where do SNOMED CT, openEHR archetypes, HL7 FHIR and queries fit in? (The 'propeller' paper)

2
00:00:48.000 --> 00:04:19.000
Terminology is just one part of the system: concept model, information/EHR model and inference model - coordinated, but not the same thing

3
00:04:19.000 --> 00:07:34.000
If doing it today: archetypes hung on a concept model? Grading and staging of cancers in a cancer trial project

4
00:07:34.000 --> 00:08:37.000
openEHR, FHIR and finding the right granularity - 'I'd certainly use SNOMED if I were starting today'

5
00:08:37.000 --> 00:14:20.000
Query SNOMED rather than create new concepts. Lessons from the ICD-11 project: statistics need stability, and ICD wouldn't work for PEN&PAD

6
00:14:20.000 --> 00:18:02.000
Building on SNOMED: watch out for primitives with more than one parent, and terminologies built by committee

7
00:18:02.000 --> 00:22:51.000
Redoing PEN&PAD today: rethink user centered design for touch screens, pens, voice and natural language - 'Is this what you meant?'

8
00:22:51.000 --> 00:26:27.000
Don't make one thing serve too many purposes (HL7 V3 prescriptions) - a flexible combination of modules

9
00:26:27.000 --> 00:29:44.000
Centering the record on the patient, and language generation for clinicians and for patients

10
00:29:44.000 --> 00:35:19.000
Sharing records between institutions and departments - find the nugget that needs to be transmitted; how do you summarize?

11
00:35:19.000 --> 00:39:58.000
Systems built out of bits and pieces - lessons from SGML and HTML ('Page not found')

12
00:39:58.000 --> 00:48:04.000
Advice to students coming into health informatics from the computer or the medical side - talk to psychologists, nurses and junior doctors

13
00:48:04.000 --> 00:49:50.000
Alan's acknowledgements: the PEN&PAD, GALEN and OWL teams

14
00:49:50.000 --> 00:49:58.240
The end
